mutation emit a disposition outside the documented diagnostic states
detects TypeOK
only one attempt
- CASE p = "recognized" -> "recorded"
+ CASE p = "recognized" -> "raw_response"

mutation schedule a diagnostic parser for another provider
detects AppleRejectionsOnly
only one attempt
- /\ diagnostic' = IF IsAppleRejection(input)
+ /\ diagnostic' = IF IsAppleRejection(input) \/ input = "other_bad"

mutation report an old rejection against the current replacement reservation
detects CapturedMetadata
only two attempts
- [meta |-> diagnostic[i].meta,
+ [meta |-> [diagnostic[i].meta EXCEPT !.reservationId = queue.active],

mutation record an unrecognized provider string verbatim
detects SafeReasons
only one attempt
- IF p = "recognized" THEN "BadTtl" ELSE "none"
+ IF p = "recognized" THEN "BadTtl" ELSE IF p = "unknown" THEN "opaque-token" ELSE "none"

mutation omit the documented reason from a valid diagnostic body
detects SafeReasons
only one attempt
- IF p = "recognized" THEN "BadTtl" ELSE "none"
+ "none"

mutation classify rejected HTTP replies as accepted in the standard log
detects DeliveryIndependent
only one attempt
- outcome |-> DeliveryOutcome(input), retry |-> Retry(input)
+ outcome |-> "provider_accepted", retry |-> Retry(input)

mutation wait for the optional reader before committing the reminder queue
detects CommitDoesNotWait
only one attempt
- /\ phase = "commit"
+ /\ phase = "commit" /\ diagnostic[count].disposition # "reading"

mutation update the queue when the diagnostic reader finishes
detects ReaderDoesNotWrite
only one attempt
- /\ UNCHANGED <<queue, phase, count, attempted, delivery>>
+ /\ queue' = NewQueue(queue.last, 0, {})
+ /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, count, attempted, delivery>>
